  "reason": "The current best is config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) at 0.713 accuracy. All other design axes have been well-explored: scvi_n200 > scgpt > pca, multiprofile >> singleprofile, transformer ≥ avgpool, and weighted > concat. The one major untested axis in the best configuration is the image encoder. ResNet50 alone was very weak (0.208), yet it still contributed ~6% over RNA-only when fused, suggesting a stronger visual encoder could yield further gains. config_039 replaces resnet50 with imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) constant, isolating the image-encoder effect. With only one experiment remaining after this, testing the highest-leverage single change to the best configuration is the most efficient use of the budget."
}

